*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# AGENTS.md.bak holds the 348-line predecessor of AGENTS.md, including the 34
# gotchas that were dropped when the file was condensed. Kept on disk as
# read-only history, deliberately NOT tracked: it is superseded, and leaving it
# untracked-but-unignored meant a `git add -A` would have swept it into some
# unrelated commit. The *.json.bak rule above covers pokemon_data.json.bak; this
# one is here because the two backups are not the same kind of file.
AGENTS.md.bak

# Agent tooling state (.opencode/plans/*.md are session scratch, not project
# artifacts; .opencode/.gitignore already covers node_modules and package.json)
.opencode/

# IDE settings
# The whole directory, not a whitelist of shared files. This repo is published, and
# .vscode/ is where editor state ends up (tasks the author never meant to share,
# launch configs with absolute paths, an extensions.json recommending the author's
# toolchain). The one file that looked like a project artifact was settings.json,
# pinning liveServer.settings.port to 5500 — but that port is Live Server's own
# default, so nothing is actually lost by not tracking it, and CRY_PORT exists for
# anyone running on a different port. Ignoring the directory leaves settings.json
# working exactly as before; it just stops being shared.
.idea/
.vscode/

# OS-generated files
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# InfoPoke reference snapshots (inputs to the generators, not vendored)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# *.json.bak is add_collection_tags.py's own pre-write backup, not an input.
*.json.bak
#
# infopoke_net_*.html are the page captures that scripts/extract_generations.py
# and scripts/add_collection_tags.py parse. They are 3.1 MB of third-party
# markup that changes whenever infopoke.net ships a redesign, so they are not
# tracked; what IS tracked is the JSON each script produces from them. Re-fetch
# a missing one from its source URL — both scripts now exit with that URL
# rather than raising FileNotFoundError. See the "InfoPoke reference snapshots"
# entry in AGENTS.md.
infopoke_net_*.html

# pokered's 114 Generation I cry .asm files. Build-time inputs to
# fetch_gen1_cries.py, which parses them into assets/data/gen1_cries.json and
# gen1_cry_sfx.json. Not tracked for the same reason as the InfoPoke captures:
# they are third-party source that changes whenever pret/pokered is rebased, and
# what is tracked is the JSON each script produces from them.
# test_check_gen1_cries.mjs mirrors them under data-sources/ on first run and
# reuses the copy; delete the directory to force a re-fetch.
data-sources/pokered-cry/

# pokeapi_evolution_chains.json is the 541-chain cache behind
# assets/data/evolution_levels.json. 473 KB of a third-party API's JSON that
# changes whenever PokeAPI ships a change, and which fetch_evolution_levels.py
# rebuilds offline from -- or refetches with --refresh. Same rule as the
# InfoPoke captures above: the JSON the script PRODUCES is tracked, the raw
# response is not.
data-sources/pokeapi_evolution_chains.json
